cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to these instances, please cite them as below."
title: "Small two-type counterexamples for maximin-share (MMS) fair division: 4, 5, 6 and 7 agents"
abstract: >-
  Instances of fair division of indivisible goods with additive positive integer
  valuations in which no allocation gives every agent her maximin share (MMS).
  Each instance has two agent types; the goods are cells of a sparse n x n grid
  whose rows sum to T under one valuation and whose columns sum to T under the
  other, so MMS = T for every agent. The series is 4 agents / 11 goods with
  T = 30 (ratio 29/30), 5 agents / 13 goods with T = 29 (28/29), 6 agents /
  15 goods with T = 28 (27/28) and 7 agents / 17 goods with T = 27 (26/27). The
  7-agent instance gives the upper bound alpha <= 26/27 on the largest alpha for
  which alpha-MMS allocations always exist, for any number of agents, improving
  39/40 from the 3-agent, 9-good instance of Feige, Sapir and Tauber (WINE 2021);
  the n-agent instances also improve the n-specific bounds 67/68 (n = 4) and
  1 - 1/n^4 (n = 5, 6, 7). Eleven goods is minimal for four agents, by Hummel
  (IJCAI 2023). Established by exact computation and reproduced by independently
  written programs of different design (literal enumeration, subset dynamic
  programming, packing certificates), with compact two-branch weight certificates
  that can be checked by hand.
authors:
  - family-names: Alexandrov
    given-names: Andrey
    email: alexandrov.home@gmail.com
date-released: 2026-09-02
